WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.780
<b>Adventure in the Land of Science</b>

3
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.620
The... The Dr. Vegapunk?

4
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.330
Really?

5
00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.090
Scream about it,
why don't you?

6
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.920
I'm your biggest fan.

7
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.080
I can't believe this.

8
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.970
I've wanted to meet
you for so long.

9
00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.890
You taught me so much.

10
00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.860
I spent two years
at your lab in Baltimore.

11
00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.510
I studied everything I
could get my hands on.

12
00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:55.750
Like everything.

13
00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.720
You got to see
the stuff I made.

14
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.400
This is a dream come true!

15
00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.450
Oh boy, oh boy, oh boy!

16
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.000
I can't believe it!

17
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.470
A giant robot!

18
00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:13.360
It's like General Franky,
but a bajillion times bigger!

19
00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.360
I wish Luffy and Chopper
were here to see it!

20
00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.970
Vegapunk is a total babe!

21
00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.980
Might I take a look
at your panties, please?

22
00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.180
How beautiful!

23
00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.400
Giant robot!

24
00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.020
Super!

25
00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:30.800
Hold on.

26
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.800
Is there something
wrong, Robin?

27
00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.410
I've never heard that
Vegapunk was a woman.

28
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.220
A young one, no less.

29
00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.620
You filthy pirates!

30
00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.970
Obviously I'm not the Stella!

31
00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.230
The Stella?

32
00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.980
I'm Punk, too!

33
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.830
Vegapunk Lilith, the evil!

34
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:53.490
<b>Lilith the Evil</b>

35
00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.130
How strange.

36
00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.020
Something's off.

37
00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.120
Anyway, our budget's
gone down the test tube.

38
00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.180
So hand over your valuables.

39
00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.470
Then I'll consider
our business complete.

40
00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.450
No way!

41
00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.180
You expect us to head right
back into that snowstorm?

42
00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:08.780
You saved us from drowning!

43
00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.360
So follow through, dammit!

44
00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.190
I wasn't trying to save you!

45
00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:16.500
And don't you even think about
trying to sail any further!

46
00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.420
I have iron-tight defenses
trained to attack all ships.

47
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.960
Let me introduce you!

48
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.080
Huh?

49
00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.090
I call them...

50
00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.990
the sea beast weapons!

51
00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.080
Are those guys
giant robots, too?

52
00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:45.540
Sweet!

53
00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.660
Okay, now I'm scared again!

54
00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:48.440
Yeah, me too!

55
00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.510
Protect me, Robin!

56
00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.850
From now on, you play
by my rules or get sunk.

57
00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.220
So move it!

58
00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.920
Fuck over your treasure!

59
00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:02.670
Okay!

60
00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.280
Lilith, what are you
doing out there?

61
00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:10.890
Same thing as always, Shaka!

62
00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.050
Why are you calling me?

63
00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.610
Are you plundering again?

64
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.070
Where is your pride
as a scientist?

65
00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.720
Pride don't pay the bills
in case you didn't know!

66
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.180
Who is she talking to?

67
00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.550
How's the view from
that high horse?

68
00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.400
Those are the Straw
Hat Pirates.

69
00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.490
They're not going
to surrender.

70
00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.120
Their captain just became
an Emperor of the Sea.

71
00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.500
And c is for cash!

72
00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:35.120
If I steal from an Emperor, think
of all the research funding I can nab!

73
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.850
I'm afraid you've made
a miscalculation.

74
00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:39.730
No, I didn't.

75
00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.490
I surrounded them
with sea beasts.

76
00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:42.550
There's no escape!

77
00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:43.860
Hear that, dimwits?

78
00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.760
You're underestimating them.

79
00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.910
Look at the swordsman
on the ship.

80
00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:53.950
He has a bounty of one billion, one
hundred and eleven million berries.

81
00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.110
That's Pirate Hunter Zoro.

82
00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.100
Notice how calm he is?

83
00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.980
That's because he knows he can kill
you in an instant from that range.

84
00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.620
The same could be said
for Demon Child Nico Robin.

85
00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.670
She's standing
right behind him.

86
00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:10.250
But there's no way they could win
against this many sea beast weapons!

87
00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.550
They don't have to.

88
00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:14.650
The strong can determine
the highest priority target.

89
00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.810
In this case, that's you.

90
00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.620
So what are those
dotes then?

91
00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:19.840
Decoys?

92
00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:21.740
Crafty bastards.

93
00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:23.890
Hey, Vegapunk!

94
00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.460
From now on, you
play by our rules.

95
00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.340
Or you're sunk.

96
00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.260
Is that a threat?

97
00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.410
Do you know who
you're talking to?

98
00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:34.290
It's fine.

99
00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.260
Bring them in so
we can speak.

100
00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.810
I happen to have
an interest in that crew.

101
00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:42.240
<b>Shaka the Just</b>

102
00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.100
You said you've been
on this island before, right?

103
00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.700
I came here when I was a kid.

104
00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.430
It was just a regular lab then.

105
00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:51.630
Glad you come back.

106
00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.040
Must be real important.

107
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.990
You said you had
business with Vegapunk?

108
00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.760
You're damn right I do.

109
00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.870
And if I can't settle it,
I'll kill him!

110
00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:03.080
What does that mean?

111
00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:06.960
What did he do wrong?

112
00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:12.450
Years ago, Vegapunk turned
my father into a cyborg.

113
00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.060
Whoa, a cyborg?

114
00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:14.950
That's so cool!

115
00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.030
Shut the hell up!

116
00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:21.600
My father had all sense
of self ripped away from him.

117
00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.750
He doesn't even know
who he is anymore.

118
00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:30.010
He became nothing more
than a living weapon.

119
00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.900
What a horrific fate.

120
00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.240
My condolences.

121
00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:34.780
He'll pay.

122
00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.160
Mark my words.

123
00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:37.830
I'm sorry, boggy.

124
00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:38.680
I didn't know.

125
00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.040
Bonney!

126
00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:43.460
Sorry again!

127
00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:46.210
Just keep moving, okay?

128
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.150
This should get
us to the surface.

129
00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.320
Sounds good.

130
00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:55.910
Hey look!

131
00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.090
I can see the exit!

132
00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:58.290
A future island!

133
00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.630
All I see in my future
is food, food, food!

134
00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:04.620
This is it!

135
00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.380
Okay, let's find
some snacks and...

136
00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:15.640
Luffy!

137
00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.170
You see something cool?

138
00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:18.250
Hey, wait for me!

139
00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.700
Probably should have told him
I saw Sabo at Mary Geoise.

140
00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:23.960
Oh well.

141
00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.080
This place is crazy!

142
00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.180
There's a giant robot!

143
00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.700
This is quite a sight.

144
00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.190
Is that a space monster?

145
00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.740
And look at all
the stuff in the sky!

146
00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:54.510
Awesome!

147
00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.330
I'm gonna ride on the red guy!

148
00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:01.020
Luffy, let's be careful!

149
00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:04.260
We need to keep
a low profile, stupid!

150
00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.400
Luffy!

151
00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:22.290
Luffy!

152
00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:23.120
Ugh...

153
00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.130
Oh, no!

154
00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:30.070
Luffy, Luffy!

155
00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.960
I thought the lizard ate me!

156
00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.690
I'm putting down.

157
00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.580
Food!

158
00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.730
Fruit and cookies!

159
00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:44.310
Hey!

160
00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:45.480
Come back here!

161
00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:46.640
It could be a trap!

162
00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.920
Lizard! Lizard! Lizard!

163
00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.500
Why can't I eat this stuff?

164
00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.830
Let me eat you!

165
00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:14.190
Help me!

166
00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:15.110
I'm starving!

167
00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:22.400
I think I figured it out!

168
00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.650
What is it?

169
00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.910
We can't touch it
because we're dead!

170
00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.730
You think we're ghosts?

171
00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:33.310
Wait a minute, Luffy!

172
00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.310
Leave it alone!

173
00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:35.390
I'm already dead!

174
00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.900
That doesn't seem
likely to me.

175
00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.280
Then why do I go
through the food?

176
00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.870
I don't think we're the ones
who are immaterial.

177
00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:44.310
Let me try something.

178
00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.190
I thought I was going to die.

179
00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:49.560
Not so.

180
00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:51.800
I'm afraid this parfait
is only a hologram.

181
00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:52.910
A holo-holo?

182
00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.220
Why are they
messing with me?

183
00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.470
I have no idea why they'd want
to litter the streets with fake food.

184
00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:03.040
But I'm not exactly
an expert on holograms.

185
00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.410
Well, I hate them!

186
00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.430
They're mean!

187
00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:06.430
They're not mean.

188
00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:08.420
Their image is
produced by light.

189
00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.810
Haven't you seen this kind
of stuff in a comic before?

190
00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:11.600
It's Sci-Fi.

191
00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:12.490
It's a liar!

192
00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.920
That must be why I went
straight through that monster!

193
00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.450
The giant robot must
be a hologram, too.

194
00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.470
No one could make
one that big.

195
00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:23.260
Guys!

196
00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:24.540
Look at this!

197
00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.080
What is this thing?

198
00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:26.960
What?

199
00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:29.960
There's pictures of food
on all the buttons!

200
00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:32.180
It's probably fake
like everything else.

201
00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:33.210
Just give it up.

202
00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:34.600
This island sucks.

203
00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.600
Something else is
strange about this place.

204
00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.950
Just a short while ago,
we were all freezing.

205
00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:43.060
But since we've arrived here,
it's been quite warm.

206
00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:43.960
Well, yeah.

207
00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:47.080
That's 'cause I set
the climate to tropical.

208
00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.200
Gotta get crafty when you
live on a winter island.

209
00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:53.940
I invented the island ac so
we could stay nice and cozy.

210
00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.960
I can control the temperature
of this whole island.

211
00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.540
The heat comes
from the ground.

212
00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:01.540
Speaking of which,
you bastards are new.

213
00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.240
Where did you come from?

214
00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:11.770
She's bigger than Kaido!

215
00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:15.130
Anyway, I don't have time to chat,
so you guys stay out of trouble,

216
00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:15.930
whoever you are.

217
00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:18.990
I'm on my way to work,
so I'd better hurry.

218
00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.190
Step aside, please.

219
00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.210
I bet you made
that fake parfait!

220
00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.760
I'm starving to death here!

221
00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.330
What's the big idea
tricking me like that?

222
00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:28.910
Oh, if you're hungry, I can...

223
00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.790
Are you a ball
of ham, too, huh?

224
00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.300
Oh, hey, I hit her!

225
00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.440
Is she real?

226
00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:36.420
Am I real?

227
00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.110
Oh, I'm real.

228
00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.910
Real pissed off!

229
00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:42.650
I'm sorry.

230
00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:50.110
She is real,
and she killed Luffy!

231
00:11:58.940 --> 00:11:59.770
Oh!

232
00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.120
Hmm...

233
00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:14.180
This texture, this smell...

234
00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:18.490
A real hamburger with real
fries and a real drink!

235
00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:20.380
Finally!

236
00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.350
Then it's not a holo-gram!

237
00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:22.050
It's real!

238
00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:22.920
Give me it!

239
00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:27.410
Yummy!

240
00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.400
It's the real deal!

241
00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:31.670
Yay!

242
00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:33.270
Wait a sec.

243
00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.400
Who made all of this?

244
00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:35.910
It came out of the thing!

245
00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:36.870
You think there's
someone in there?

246
00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.400
He just hit a button
and food popped out!

247
00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.040
Then what the hell
are we waiting for?

248
00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:42.480
Let's start pushing
some buttons!

249
00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:43.450
Heck yeah!

250
00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:43.940
Ooh, steak!

251
00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:45.420
Eggs and a pork cutlet!

252
00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:49.450
Yummy!

253
00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.500
Let's do desserts!

254
00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.420
No, pizza!

255
00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.600
I know what I want!

256
00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:58.140
Ramen, fried chicken,
and a hot dog!

257
00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.390
Oh, press them all at once
so they come out faster!

258
00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:01.720
Oh, yeah, nice thinking!

259
00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:02.510
Of course!

260
00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:03.750
Chopper's a genius!

261
00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:06.140
Flattery doesn't make
me happy, you bastard!

262
00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.420
Whatcha want, Jinbe?

263
00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.290
I'll pass.

264
00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:09.170
Thank you.

265
00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:18.340
Wow, Bonney.

266
00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.420
You sure eat a lot.

267
00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:20.890
I said I was hungry.

268
00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:22.760
And you're eating
as much as me!

269
00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.320
I was hungry, too!

270
00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.640
Yeah, and I was, too!

271
00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.760
Looks like my invention
is a big hit.

272
00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:32.150
What am I looking at?

273
00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:33.570
What is that thing?

274
00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:34.830
You're curious, huh?

275
00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:39.460
Behold my auto-cooking
machine!

276
00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:45.080
As long as there are enough ingredients, it
can prepare 500 different dishes per minute!

277
00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.140
It even has a Whip
Up Leftovers mode.

278
00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.100
It's gonna change the world!

279
00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:53.540
Or it would change the world.

280
00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.520
If we can mass produce it!

281
00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:59.000
But no, we don't have the budget
to hire technicians for that!

282
00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.550
Same with the island A.c.!

283
00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.840
We could use its temperature
technology to track everything!

284
00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:06.260
Everyone on the island,
but we don't have the money!

285
00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:09.560
Every damn day, I build
world-shattering new inventions!

286
00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:13.180
And every damn day,
I get screwed by budget cuts!

287
00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:15.620
If I had the money,
I could do anything!

288
00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:17.520
Even control the weather!

289
00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:20.790
The world needs my technology,
and I need cash!

290
00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:24.830
I'm doing my part,
why can't they do theirs?

291
00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.460
It makes me so...

292
00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:32.320
Where's my freaking
minutes?!

293
00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:36.640
No way!

294
00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:37.950
She punched a hologram?!

295
00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:41.460
Right trip, yeah!

296
00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:40.150
It waffles!

297
00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.390
I'm better now!

298
00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:49.140
How did you
punch that thing?

299
00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.910
I thought everything
here was a hologram.

300
00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:53.080
Still curious?

301
00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.800
Then listen closely!

302
00:14:54.880 --> 00:15:00.000
With these light pressure gloves,
I can do more than just observe holograms!

303
00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:01.920
Hi!

304
00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.180
What happens when
someone touches an object?

305
00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.220
They perceive it as
real, don't they?

306
00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.420
So she's not real?

307
00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:10.220
No way!

308
00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.720
Shall we find out?

309
00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:15.110
Luffy, watch out!

310
00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.440
She wasn't real after all!

311
00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:25.180
I don't know what can kill
me and what can't anymore!

312
00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:26.840
What decides if she's real?

313
00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:28.240
If anything is.

314
00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.540
That's for you
to determine on your own.

315
00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:33.120
Rigid thinking needs
to become a thing of the past!

316
00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:34.340
That's what I say!

317
00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:36.100
She's still inside me!

318
00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:40.710
Perhaps I should have asked
sooner, but who are you?

319
00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.530
Me?

320
00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:47.090
Nothing but a humble,
genius scientist for hire!

321
00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:54.600
Doctor... Vegapunk!

322
00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.900
<b>Atlas the Enraged</b>

323
00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:00.650
Yum!

324
00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:04.860
You're Doctor Vegapunk?!

325
00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:06.620
Koby told me about you!

326
00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:08.220
How come you're
a giant kid?!

327
00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.640
What the hell is
this liar talking about?

328
00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:14.160
<b>New World</b>

329
00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:19.510
So, what's our next move?

330
00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.300
Here's what we know.

331
00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:24.110
There's only one man
with a mind like Vegapunk's.

332
00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:27.190
And a genius like that
always has a full plate.

333
00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:31.210
Of course, he could use some help
with his work, but no one else can keep up.

334
00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.690
With that thought in mind,
he had an idea.

335
00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:36.680
What if he split himself
into six different people?

336
00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.320
Those offshoots
are called satellites.

337
00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:45.810
<b>Dr. Vegapunk</b>

338
00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:37.260
<b>Justice Evil Vision</b>

339
00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:37.050
<b>Punk
01 Punk
02</b>
<b>Shaka Lilith</b>

340
00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:37.260
<b>Punk
01 Punk
02 Punk
03</b>
<b>Shaka Lilith Edison</b>

341
00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.140
<b>Justice Evil Vision Wisdom Rage Greed</b>

342
00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:37.470
<b>Punk
01 Punk
02 Punk
03 Punk
04 Punk
05</b>

343
00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:44.350
<b>Shaka Lilith Edison Pythagoras Atlas York</b>

344
00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:44.350
<b>Punk
01 Punk
02 Punk
03 Punk
04 Punk
05 Punk
06</b>

345
00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:44.350
<b>Justice Evil Vision Wisdom Rage Greed</b>

346
00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:42.730
The satellites function
as their own individuals.

347
00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:46.030
But at the end of the day,
they're all Vegapunk.

348
00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.810
<b>Punk
01 Punk
02 Punk
03 Punk
04 Punk
05 Punk
06</b>
<b>Justice Evil Vision Wisdom Rage Greed</b>
<b>Shaka Lilith Edison Pythagoras Atlas York</b>

349
00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:50.480
If you weren't the one telling me,
I'd say this was too insane to be true.

350
00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:52.440
Six geniuses.

351
00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:53.920
This will be a pain.

352
00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.020
So we make
our way to Egghead.

353
00:16:56.950 --> 00:17:02.880
<b>Kaku, Lucci, and Stussy</b>
<b>Cipher Pol Aigis 0
(Masked Assassins)</b>

354
00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.960
We tell them we're
returning this.

355
00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:02.130
And once we're in, we
kill all of the Vegapunks.

356
00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:04.790
Yes, but his lab's full
of priceless research.

357
00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.970
Let's try to keep
the damage to a minimum.

358
00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:10.750
They want us to eliminate
the most useful man in the world.

359
00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.450
Does this have something
to do with Lulusia?

360
00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:15.650
Considering
the timing, it must.

361
00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.020
Lulusia, you're a smart boy.

362
00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:21.270
You should know better than
to be nosy about these things.

363
00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:22.430
Listen to her, Lucci.

364
00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.060
Trouble for you means
trouble for all of us.

365
00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:25.850
Let it go.

366
00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:26.630
Uh-huh.

367
00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.390
It was so good.

368
00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:32.580
Too bad everyone
else missed out.

369
00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.220
Guess we'll have to eat again.

370
00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.570
I can't wait to show
them the food machine.

371
00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:38.600
They're gonna love it for sure.

372
00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.550
Well, Sanji might
not be too happy.

373
00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:43.340
You sure made a big mess.

374
00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:46.270
And those bellies, they look
like they're about to burst.

375
00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:47.920
I always look like this.

376
00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:51.090
<b>Recycollie</b>

377
00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:55.470
Gotta work.

378
00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:56.170
Bye.

379
00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:58.190
Wait, what's your job?

380
00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:00.520
Oh, you know, just
violence and stuff.

381
00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:01.950
I'm sorry, what?

382
00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:20.270
Are those robots, too?

383
00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:22.980
This place is a lab, isn't it?

384
00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.900
My guess is that
they're researchers.

385
00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:28.500
There wasn't anyone in town at first,
but now there's a whole crowd.

386
00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.580
Now on.

387
00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:32.620
Perhaps they were waiting
to see if we posed a threat.

388
00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:34.230
Their clothes look so heavy.

389
00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:36.570
Aren't they too hot
in this weather?

390
00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:37.520
Wait a sec.

391
00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.340
Where'd Luffy go?

392
00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.240
That sounded
like Luffy's voice.

393
00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:45.960
What are you doing?

394
00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:47.520
Give me my hat back!

395
00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:50.130
Luffy!

396
00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:52.100
What's he doing in there?

397
00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:55.890
Hey, guys.

398
00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.350
What do you think?

399
00:18:57.430 --> 00:18:58.480
Do you like it?

400
00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:05.310
I love how this feels.

401
00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.460
It looks kind of heavy.

402
00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.110
It's actually not at all.

403
00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:11.070
And it's cool inside.

404
00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:13.520
You look quite nice.

405
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:14.660
I want one.

406
00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:16.820
You got the clothes in there?

407
00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:17.920
Yeah, go on in.

408
00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.040
Free food and free clothes?

409
00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.060
The future is so handy.

410
00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:25.580
I do feel a little sticky
thanks to that sea water.

411
00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:26.660
Welcome.

412
00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.920
Please choose
your preferred clothing style.

413
00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:30.370
In that case...

414
00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:32.980
Come back here!

415
00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:38.840
I can get dressed
myself, okay?

416
00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:42.500
He was...

417
00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:46.990
right.

418
00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:48.520
I'm as light as a feather.

419
00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.250
I feel like I'm floating
in these shoes.

420
00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.150
This is great!

421
00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:54.380
The future.

422
00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:56.830
I'm glad they had
something tropical, too.

423
00:19:56.830 --> 00:19:57.700
Oh, yeah.

424
00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:00.110
You look amazing, Jinbe.

425
00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:00.680
Okay?

426
00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:01.160
Thank you.

427
00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.290
Hopefully this will
help us blend in.

428
00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:05.710
Although it might
be too late for that.

429
00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:08.670
I'm going to go
and look for a weapon.

430
00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:10.420
Then I'm going to try
to find Vegapunk.

431
00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:11.310
So I'm off.

432
00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:12.560
See you around.

433
00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.120
Stay safe out there, Bonney!

434
00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:16.410
Yeah, good luck!

435
00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:25.680
Wait!

436
00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.510
It's Kuma.

437
00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:32.640
Really?

438
00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:33.890
It could be trouble.

439
00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:35.630
Is he looking for us?

440
00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:40.600
Let's go!

441
00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:41.510
Huh?

442
00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.060
Gotta run for it, guys!

443
00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:46.890
He's definitely coming for us!

444
00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:47.670
Wait!

445
00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:54.320
Could you tell me who we're
running away from and why?

446
00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:55.580
Later, okay?

447
00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:58.230
Dammit, no!

448
00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.220
Aggravated theft
of food and clothing.

449
00:21:12.530 --> 00:21:14.520
Watch out!

450
00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:15.560
He's gonna fire!

451
00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:25.620
The thing didn't
ask for money!

452
00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:26.930
It worked when I hit it!

453
00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:28.790
That sounds like
vandalism to me!

454
00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:36.150
This is crazy!

455
00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:37.610
He's trying to kill us!

456
00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.240
The law here is quite harsh.

457
00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.290
Looks like he's going all out!

458
00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:46.470
We gotta fight back!

459
00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:50.200
Yes, we may be pirates,
but self-defense is self-defense!

460
00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.090
Let's go!

461
00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:52.400
I'm sorry, Kuma!

462
00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:53.750
Gah!

463
00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.840
Aaaah!

464
00:21:56.820 --> 00:21:57.620
Aaaaaaaaaah!

465
00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:13.080
Alright!

466
00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:13.680
Gum...

467
00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:14.480
Gum!

468
00:22:22.170 --> 00:22:23.670
Stop it!

469
00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:36.330
What's your deal, Bonney?

470
00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:38.250
He's using lasers on us!

471
00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:40.070
Can I at least hit him?

472
00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:50.670
He's my father.

473
00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:56.610
He's all I've got.

474
00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:01.520
He's the only family I have.

475
00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:11.560
When you said your dad
got turned into a cyborg...

476
00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:13.540
You were talking
about Kuma?

477
00:23:32.420 --> 00:23:33.660
This isn't his fault!

478
00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:37.030
So don't hurt my father,
I'm begging you!

479
00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:38.870
Run away, you dummy!

480
00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:40.180
That's a pacifista!

481
00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:45.690
Bonney!

482
00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:56.250
<b>A Stretch of Sea
New World</b>

483
00:24:03.800 --> 00:24:05.450
Close valve two, quick!

484
00:24:06.230 --> 00:24:07.410
We need cover here!

485
00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:09.050
Here, you!

486
00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:14.230
I see something dead ahead!

487
00:24:14.310 --> 00:24:15.400
Turn now!

488
00:24:21.240 --> 00:24:22.690
It's no use, Captain!

489
00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:23.820
We can't escape!

490
00:24:36.070 --> 00:24:37.910
Come out and fight me!

491
00:24:48.670 --> 00:24:50.100
We can't take another hit!

492
00:24:50.180 --> 00:24:52.210
The water pressure's
gonna crush the sub!

493
00:24:52.210 --> 00:24:54.290
Captain, you gotta
make the call!

494
00:24:59.380 --> 00:25:00.210
Let's surface.

495
00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:03.100
To the northeast, near land!

496
00:25:03.180 --> 00:25:04.580
Aye aye, Captain!

497
00:25:07.280 --> 00:25:08.560
Hard to starboard!

498
00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:17.230
Everyone get ready to fight!

499
00:25:17.310 --> 00:25:18.090
Let's go!

500
00:25:22.030 --> 00:25:22.730
Dammit.

501
00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:24.450
Must be a devil fruit power.

502
00:25:24.820 --> 00:25:26.140
We're in their trap.

503
00:25:26.220 --> 00:25:27.220
Be careful!

504
00:25:27.300 --> 00:25:28.500
I, cutie.

505
00:25:28.580 --> 00:25:29.660
I mean, Captain.

506
00:25:29.740 --> 00:25:32.330
If you don't shut
your mouths, I'll gut you!

507
00:25:32.960 --> 00:25:34.840
You're cute when
you're mad, too!

508
00:25:36.860 --> 00:25:37.700
Oh no!

509
00:25:37.780 --> 00:25:39.400
I've been girlified!

510
00:25:41.240 --> 00:25:43.360
It's spreading
to the entire crew!

511
00:25:43.440 --> 00:25:45.510
Then stay away
from the infected!

512
00:25:45.590 --> 00:25:46.290
Oops.

513
00:25:46.330 --> 00:25:47.130
Sorry.

514
00:25:47.610 --> 00:25:49.910
It's functioning like
a contagious disease.

515
00:25:49.990 --> 00:25:51.860
How are they
changing our sex?

516
00:25:53.880 --> 00:25:54.710
Never mind.

517
00:25:56.120 --> 00:25:58.470
I learned something
fighting an Emperor.

518
00:25:59.160 --> 00:26:00.630
I can break through this!

519
00:26:01.070 --> 00:26:02.960
You intensify your haki!

520
00:26:03.040 --> 00:26:05.070
It nullifies devil fruit powers!

521
00:26:20.610 --> 00:26:22.670
We've reached
the surface, Captain!

522
00:26:23.420 --> 00:26:24.250
I'm okay!

523
00:26:25.190 --> 00:26:28.230
I did it.

524
00:26:28.310 --> 00:26:30.760
There's no power
you can't beat!

525
00:26:30.840 --> 00:26:32.990
We can celebrate when
we've won this fight.

526
00:26:33.030 --> 00:26:35.100
Doctor Sub,
we're going ashore!

527
00:26:35.180 --> 00:26:36.570
Aye aye, sir!

528
00:26:42.440 --> 00:26:45.440
Seems he cured
the disease already.

529
00:26:45.520 --> 00:26:48.400
He's worth three billion
for a reason, I suppose.

530
00:26:48.480 --> 00:26:49.440
Handy trick.

531
00:26:49.520 --> 00:26:53.550
As soon as he broke through the illness,
his antibodies spread as quickly

532
00:26:53.630 --> 00:26:54.550
as the contagion.

533
00:26:56.070 --> 00:26:58.040
But it was fun while it lasted.

534
00:26:58.120 --> 00:27:00.020
My feminization disease.

535
00:26:59.890 --> 00:27:02.350
<b>Doc Q</b>
<b>(Sick-Sick Fruit)</b>

536
00:27:04.190 --> 00:27:07.210
Burgess, I'll move
us to the island.

537
00:27:07.060 --> 00:27:09.570
<b>Van Augur</b>
<b>(Warp-Warp Fruit)</b>

538
00:27:09.290 --> 00:27:10.290
Hell yeah!

539
00:27:14.070 --> 00:27:14.870
Guys,

540
00:27:21.770 --> 00:27:23.280
Is that mountain moving?

541
00:27:24.650 --> 00:27:26.470
There's someone lifting it off!

542
00:27:30.630 --> 00:27:31.460
Grr.

543
00:27:36.850 --> 00:27:37.680
Wee!

544
00:27:39.770 --> 00:27:41.050
This is true power!

545
00:27:41.130 --> 00:27:43.030
Thanks to the
Strong-Strong Fruit!

546
00:27:43.100 --> 00:27:45.560
<b>Jesus Burgess</b>
<b>(Strong-Strong Fruit)</b>

547
00:27:45.280 --> 00:27:47.040
Is that Burgess?

548
00:27:47.120 --> 00:27:48.080
So what?

549
00:27:48.160 --> 00:27:50.380
He can just toss around
whole mountains now?

550
00:27:50.460 --> 00:27:53.530
And how did he manage to get
to the shore so quickly?

551
00:27:53.610 --> 00:27:55.580
They're using Devil
Fruit powers.

552
00:27:56.010 --> 00:27:59.270
Teleportation, contagion,
superhuman strength.

553
00:27:59.810 --> 00:28:02.970
They must have gained these
by hunting for specific abilities.

554
00:28:03.050 --> 00:28:05.230
I see why their bounties
keep rising.

555
00:28:16.320 --> 00:28:17.870
Room!

556
00:28:23.810 --> 00:28:25.350
Amputate!

557
00:28:55.640 --> 00:29:00.230
It's been a while,
hasn't it, Trafalgar Law?

558
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:02.710
What is this, Blackbeard?

559
00:29:02.790 --> 00:29:04.040
What do you want from us?

560
00:29:04.080 --> 00:29:05.440
Don't be so cold!

561
00:29:05.520 --> 00:29:08.240
We're both in the worst
generation, aren't we?

562
00:29:13.160 --> 00:29:14.000
Commodore!

563
00:29:15.060 --> 00:29:17.590
Stronger says you're
a bit too heavy.

564
00:29:18.030 --> 00:29:19.240
And I agree!

565
00:29:22.320 --> 00:29:24.700
<b>Stronger</b>
<b>(Horse-Horse Fruit: Pegasus
Mythical Type)</b>

566
00:29:24.790 --> 00:29:27.320
I knew someone would be
coming through here from Wano.

567
00:29:27.320 --> 00:29:31.040
I wasn't sure if it would be you,
Straw Hat, or Kid, but that's fine,

568
00:29:31.120 --> 00:29:32.180
I'm not picky.

569
00:29:32.720 --> 00:29:35.680
I can't believe you took
out Kaido and Big Bob.

570
00:29:35.760 --> 00:29:38.230
You turned the whole
world upside down.

571
00:29:38.310 --> 00:29:39.970
Feels good, don't it?

572
00:29:43.940 --> 00:29:47.620
I bet you got a fine
treasure from Kaido, right?

573
00:29:49.530 --> 00:29:52.200
How many Road Poneglyphs
do you have now?

574
00:29:52.280 --> 00:29:56.420
I can't wait to find out,
cause soon they'll all be mine.

575
00:29:59.970 --> 00:30:01.740
I could say the same to you.

576
00:30:08.040 --> 00:30:09.710
So let's do this!

577
00:30:10.270 --> 00:30:12.210
Winner takes all!
